---
/*
 * DataverseArchitectureDecisionGuide.astro
 *
 * Purpose:
 * Helps readers choose an appropriate Dataverse or integration
 * architecture pattern for a workload.
 *
 * This component is a reasoning aid. It does not replace a full
 * architecture, security, performance, capacity, or licensing review.
 */
---

<section
  class="dadg"
  data-dadg
  aria-labelledby="dadg-title"
>
  <div class="dadg__header">
    <div class="dadg__header-copy">
      <p class="dadg__eyebrow">Architecture decision guide</p>

      <h3 id="dadg-title">
        Which Dataverse pattern fits the workload?
      </h3>

      <p class="dadg__intro">
        Start with the workload rather than the technology. Choose the scenario
        that best describes what the data needs to do, then use the suggested
        pattern as the starting point for architecture review.
      </p>
    </div>

    <span
      class="dadg__badge"
      data-badge
      aria-live="polite"
    >
      Choose a workload
    </span>
  </div>

  <fieldset class="dadg__choices">
    <legend class="dadg__legend">
      Select the scenario that best matches your workload
    </legend>

    <label class="dadg__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="dataverse-architecture-pattern"
        value="transactional"
      />

      <span
        class="dadg__marker dadg__marker--green"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span></span>
      </span>

      <span class="dadg__choice-body">
        <strong>Transactional business data</strong>

        <span>
          The workload needs governed relational business data, strong
          relationships, business rules, security, and application lifecycle
          support.
        </span>

        <small>
          RELATIONAL · OPERATIONAL · GOVERNED
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dadg__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="dataverse-architecture-pattern"
        value="high-volume"
      />

      <span
        class="dadg__marker dadg__marker--purple"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span></span>
      </span>

      <span class="dadg__choice-body">
        <strong>High-volume or bursty data</strong>

        <span>
          The workload produces high-volume, semi-structured, or bursty
          operational data where partitioning and workload-specific scale
          matter.
        </span>

        <small>
          HIGH VOLUME · PARTITIONED · SEMI-STRUCTURED
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dadg__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="dataverse-architecture-pattern"
        value="external-authority"
      />

      <span
        class="dadg__marker dadg__marker--blue"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span></span>
      </span>

      <span class="dadg__choice-body">
        <strong>External system remains authoritative</strong>

        <span>
          Another platform owns the source data and the application needs
          Dataverse-style access without creating another operational copy.
        </span>

        <small>
          EXTERNAL SYSTEM OF RECORD · NO PRIMARY REPLICATION
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dadg__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="dataverse-architecture-pattern"
        value="analytics"
      />

      <span
        class="dadg__marker dadg__marker--teal"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span></span>
      </span>

      <span class="dadg__choice-body">
        <strong>Analytics or AI workload</strong>

        <span>
          The workload needs analytical scale, semantic models, reporting, or
          AI-oriented data products rather than transactional API processing.
        </span>

        <small>
          ANALYTICS · FABRIC / ONELAKE · AI
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="dadg__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="dataverse-architecture-pattern"
        value="business-operation"
      />

      <span
        class="dadg__marker dadg__marker--orange"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <span></span>
      </span>

      <span class="dadg__choice-body">
        <strong>Business operation or domain logic</strong>

        <span>
          The application needs a governed business operation that should be
          exposed to code, automation, or event-driven processing.
        </span>

        <small>
          CUSTOM API · PLUG-IN · EVENTS · AUTOMATION
        </small>
      </span>
    </label>
  </fieldset>

  <div
    class="dadg__result"
    aria-live="polite"
    aria-atomic="true"
  >
    <div class="dadg__result-head">
      <div>
        <span class="dadg__result-kicker">
          Starting recommendation
        </span>

        <h4 data-title>
          Choose a workload above.
        </h4>
      </div>

      <span
        class="dadg__result-level"
        data-level
      >
        Waiting for selection
      </span>
    </div>

    <p
      class="dadg__result-description"
      data-description
    >
      The recommendation will identify a likely Dataverse or integration
      pattern and the main architectural question to validate next.
    </p>

    <div class="dadg__grid">
      <div class="dadg__card">
        <span class="dadg__card-label">
          Suggested pattern
        </span>

        <strong data-pattern>
          Select a workload.
        </strong>
      </div>

      <div class="dadg__card">
        <span class="dadg__card-label">
          Why it fits
        </span>

        <strong data-fit>
          The guide will explain the architectural match.
        </strong>
      </div>

      <div class="dadg__card">
        <span class="dadg__card-label">
          Review next
        </span>

        <strong data-next>
          Validate security, performance, capacity, integration, and ALM.
        </strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="dadg__principle">
    <span
      class="dadg__principle-mark"
      aria-hidden="true"
    >
      →
    </span>

    <p>
      <strong>Start with the system of record.</strong>
      Dataverse is a strong fit for governed operational business data, while
      other patterns are more appropriate when external systems, analytical
      scale, or high-volume workloads drive the architecture.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const roots = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(
    "[data-dadg]"
  );

  roots.forEach((root) => {
    if (root.dataset.initialized === "true") {
      return;
    }

    root.dataset.initialized = "true";

    const badge =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-badge]");

    const title =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-title]");

    const level =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-level]");

    const description =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-description]");

    const pattern =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-pattern]");

    const fit =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-fit]");

    const next =
      root.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-next]");

    const choices = Array.from(
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>(
        'input[name="dataverse-architecture-pattern"]'
      )
    );

    if (
      !badge ||
      !title ||
      !level ||
      !description ||
      !pattern ||
      !fit ||
      !next
    ) {
      return;
    }

    const results = {
      transactional: {
        badge: "TRANSACTIONAL",
        level: "Dataverse-first candidate",
        title:
          "Standard or custom Dataverse tables are the natural starting point.",
        description:
          "The workload is centered on governed operational business data with relational structure, security, business rules, APIs, and application lifecycle requirements.",
        pattern:
          "Standard or custom Dataverse tables",
        fit:
          "Dataverse is designed for relational business data that sits behind Power Apps, Power Automate, Power Pages, Dynamics 365, and related workloads.",
        next:
          "Validate the schema, relationships, security model, expected volume, integrations, capacity, and ALM."
      },

      "high-volume": {
        badge: "HIGH VOLUME",
        level: "Elastic-table candidate",
        title:
          "Evaluate Elastic Tables for the high-volume workload.",
        description:
          "The workload is characterized by bursty or high-volume semi-structured data where partitioning and workload-specific scale are important.",
        pattern:
          "Elastic Tables",
        fit:
          "Elastic Tables are intended for high-volume, partitioned, semi-structured workloads and have different consistency and transaction characteristics from standard tables.",
        next:
          "Design the partition key early and validate consistency, transaction needs, retention, query patterns, and operational behavior."
      },

      "external-authority": {
        badge: "EXTERNAL SYSTEM OF RECORD",
        level: "Virtual-table candidate",
        title:
          "Consider Virtual Tables when the external system remains authoritative.",
        description:
          "The workload needs Dataverse-style access to data that should remain owned by another system rather than being copied into Dataverse as the primary record.",
        pattern:
          "Virtual Tables / external-data pattern",
        fit:
          "Virtual Tables can surface external data through the Dataverse experience without making Dataverse the authoritative storage location.",
        next:
          "Validate supported capabilities, security, search, auditing, integration behavior, and the limitations of a non-persisted data model."
      },

      analytics: {
        badge: "ANALYTICS / AI",
        level: "Analytics offload",
        title:
          "Keep analytical workloads away from transactional Dataverse APIs.",
        description:
          "The workload is primarily analytical, reporting-oriented, or intended to support AI and data products rather than operational transactions.",
        pattern:
          "Fabric / OneLake analytical pattern",
        fit:
          "Fabric and OneLake provide a more appropriate analytical path for large-scale reporting, semantic models, and AI-oriented data workloads.",
        next:
          "Define the data movement or linking pattern, freshness requirements, semantic model, governance, and analytical ownership."
      },

      "business-operation": {
        badge: "BUSINESS OPERATION",
        level: "Extensibility candidate",
        title:
          "Expose the business operation through a governed server-side pattern.",
        description:
          "The workload needs a reusable business operation that should be callable by applications, automation, or event-driven integrations.",
        pattern:
          "Custom API / Plug-in / Event endpoint",
        fit:
          "Custom APIs and plug-ins can encapsulate business logic, while webhooks or Service Bus support event-driven integration when asynchronous processing is more appropriate.",
        next:
          "Choose synchronous versus asynchronous execution, define idempotency and retry behavior, and validate latency and transaction boundaries."
      }
    };

    choices.forEach((choice) => {
      choice.addEventListener("change", () => {
        const result =
          results[
            choice.value as keyof typeof results
          ];

        if (!result) {
          return;
        }

        root.dataset.state = choice.value;

        badge.textContent = result.badge;
        level.textContent = result.level;
        title.textContent = result.title;
        description.textContent = result.description;
        pattern.textContent = result.pattern;
        fit.textContent = result.fit;
        next.textContent = result.next;
      });
    });
  });
</script>

<style>
  .dadg {
    --dadg-surface: var(--surface-primary, #ffffff);
    --dadg-surface-soft: var(--surface-secondary, #f8fafc);
    --dadg-text: var(--text-primary, #0f172a);
    --dadg-text-secondary: var(--text-secondary, #475569);
    --dadg-text-tertiary: var(--text-tertiary, #64748b);
    --dadg-border: var(--border-default, #dbe3ec);
    --dadg-border-soft: var(--border-subtle, #e7edf4);
    --dadg-accent: var(--color-accent, #4ea1e0);
    --dadg-state: var(--dadg-accent);

    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--space-10, 2.5rem);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--dadg-text);
    background: var(--dadg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--dadg-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 0.875rem);
    box-shadow:
      var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .dadg[data-state="transactional"] {
    --dadg-state: var(--color-success, #15803d);
  }

  .dadg[data-state="high-volume"] {
    --dadg-state: #7c3aed;
  }

  .dadg[data-state="external-authority"] {
    --dadg-state: var(--color-accent, #4ea1e0);
  }

  .dadg[data-state="analytics"] {
    --dadg-state: var(--color-info, #0f8a8a);
  }

  .dadg[data-state="business-operation"] {
    --dadg-state: #c2410c;
  }

  .dadg__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
  }

  .dadg__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    color: var(--dadg-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .dadg h3,
  .dadg h4,
  .dadg p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .dadg h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .dadg__intro {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--dadg-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .dadg__badge {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    color: var(--dadg-state);
    background: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--dadg-state) 8%,
      var(--dadg-surface)
    );
    border: 1px solid color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--dadg-state) 30%,
      var(--dadg-border)
    );
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .dadg__choices {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3, 0.75rem);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }

  .dadg__legend {
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--dadg-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .dadg__choice {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: var(--dadg-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--dadg-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      border-color 160ms ease,
      background-color 160ms ease,
      box-shadow 160ms ease,
      transform 160ms ease;
  }

  .dadg__choice:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--dadg-accent);
    box-shadow:
      var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .dadg__choice:has(input:focus-visible) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--dadg-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .dadg__choice input {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .dadg__choice:has(input:checked) {
    border-color: var(--dadg-state);
    background: color-mix(
      in srgb,
      var(--dadg-state) 8%,
      var(--dadg-surface)
    );
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 1px var(--dadg-state),
      var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .dadg__marker {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.2rem;
    height: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--dadg-text-tertiary);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .dadg__marker span {
    width: 0.48rem;
    height: 0.48rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .dadg__choice:has(input:checked) .dadg__marker {
    border-color: var(--dadg-state);
  }

  .dadg__choice:has(input:checked) .dadg__marker span {
    background: var(--dadg-state);
  }

  .dadg__choice-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .dadg__choice-body strong {
    color: var(--dadg-text);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .dadg__choice-body > span {
    color: var(--dadg-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .dadg__choice-body small {
    color: var(--dadg-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .dadg__result {
    margin-top: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
    padding: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--dadg-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--dadg-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--dadg-state);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .dadg__result-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .dadg__result-kicker {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--dadg-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .dadg__result h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--dadg-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .dadg__result-level {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--dadg-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: right;
  }

  .dadg__result-description {
    max-width: 74ch;
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
    color: var(--dadg-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .dadg__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3, 0.75rem);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .dadg__card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.9rem;
    background: var(--dadg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--dadg-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 0.5rem);
  }

  .dadg__card-label {
    color: var(--dadg-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .dadg__card strong {
    color: var(--dadg-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .dadg__principle {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    background: var(--dadg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--dadg-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .dadg__principle-mark {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--dadg-accent);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .dadg__principle p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--dadg-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .dadg__choices,
    .dadg__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .dadg {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .dadg__header {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.9rem;
    }

    .dadg__badge {
      justify-self: start;
    }

    .dadg__result-head {
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }

    .dadg__result-level {
      text-align: left;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .dadg__choice {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
